From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HarmonyOS Porting <porting@harmonyos.org>
Date: Wed, 1 Apr 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] configure.ac: fix uuid.h detection for HarmonyOS

On HarmonyOS, uuid.h may not exist but uuid/uuid.h does (provided by
the musl-based SDK). The current configure.ac unconditionally
AC_DEFINE([HAVE_UUID_H], [1]) when libuuid is found via pkg-config,
which fails to compile when only uuid/uuid.h is available.

Fix: Replace the unconditional AC_DEFINE with AC_CHECK_HEADERS that
tries uuid.h first and falls back to uuid/uuid.h, defining the
appropriate preprocessor macro for each case.
---
 configure.ac | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -3708,7 +3708,7 @@ AS_VAR_IF([have_uuid], [missing], [
       [dnl linux-util's libuuid has uuid_generate_time_safe() since v2.20 (2011)
       dnl and provides <uuid.h>.
       have_uuid=yes
-      AC_DEFINE([HAVE_UUID_H], [1])
+      AC_CHECK_HEADERS([uuid.h], [AC_DEFINE([HAVE_UUID_H], [1])], [AC_CHECK_HEADERS([uuid/uuid.h], [AC_DEFINE([HAVE_UUID_UUID_H], [1])])])
       AC_DEFINE([HAVE_UUID_GENERATE_TIME_SAFE], [1])
     ], [
       WITH_SAVE_ENV([
